<title>JAPAN: Mimasu Semicon to change unit of trading.</title>
<headline>Mimasu Semicon to change unit of trading.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-07-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mimasu Semiconductor Industry Co Ltd said on Friday that it would change the trading unit of its shares to 100 shares from the current 1,000 shares in an attempt to attract more investors.</p>
<p>The change should take effect as of October 1, but needs to win the approval of a shareholders' meeting on August 28, the Japanese trading company specialising in silicon wafers said in a statement.</p>
<p>Following the change, Mimasu's trading unit on the Tokyo Stock Exchange will be changed to 100 shares from current 1,000 shares, it said.</p>
</text>
